{
  "number": 34,
  "title": "Add a version-consistency test between CMake PROJECT_VERSION and header version constants",
  "state": "open",
  "labels": [
    "enhancement"
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-11-16T21:18:56Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-16T21:19:39Z",
  "html_url": "https://github.com/danielm5/tiffcraft/issues/34",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe library carries two independent version sources:\n\n- `CMakeLists.txt`: `project(TiffCraft VERSION 0.1.0)` (i.e. `PROJECT_VERSION`).\n- `include/tiffcraft/TiffImage.hpp`: `MAJOR_VERSION` / `MINOR_VERSION` / `PATCH_VERSION` (currently 0.2.0).\n\nThey are intentionally kept separate so the headers remain self-contained and copyable without CMake (see #31). The cost of that separation is that a version bump can be applied to one and forgotten in the other — there is no automated check catching the drift. Issue #30's export path (`TiffCraftConfigVersion.cmake`) makes the CMake side observable, which is what surfaced the current mismatch.\n\n## Requested changes\n\nAdd an automated test that fails if the two version sources disagree. The test should:\n\n1. Compile a small program that includes `<tiffcraft/TiffImage.hpp>` and prints `TiffCraft::MAJOR_VERSION`, `MINOR_VERSION`, `PATCH_VERSION` (i.e. the output of `TiffCraft::version()`).\n2. Compare that output against `${PROJECT_VERSION}` (or its major/minor/patch components).\n3. Fail the build/test step on mismatch, with a message naming both values so the discrepancy is obvious.\n\nA CTest test is the natural fit, consistent with the existing test layout (doctest executables under `tests/`). A configure-time check (e.g. `try_compile` + run) is also acceptable if it fails earlier. Keep it standalone-build only — the test is about the library's own version, not consumption.\n\n## Context\n\n- Current mismatch: CMake reports 0.1.0, header reports 0.2.0.\n- The versions are deliberately not unified: unifying would require CMake at build time and break the copy-only consumption path documented in #31.\n- The test is the safety net for that deliberate separation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A failing test is added that would fail on the current state (0.1.0 vs 0.2.0) and pass once the two are aligned.\n- The test runs as part of the normal `ctest` invocation (or configure step) on standalone builds.\n- The test message names both the CMake and header version values on failure.\n- No change to the header or CMake version sources themselves; this issue is test-only.\n\n## Note on making the test pass\n\nThe test will fail on the current state (CMake 0.1.0 vs header 0.2.0). To make it pass, `project(TiffCraft VERSION ...)` in `CMakeLists.txt` must be updated to `0.2.0` to match the header constants — i.e. the next release is 0.2.0, not 0.1.1. This version bump is in scope for this issue (it is what makes the new test green), and is consistent with the unreleased 0.2.0 work already recorded in the CHANGELOG.",
  "author": {
    "login": "danielm5"
  },
  "assignee": null,
  "closed": false
}
